@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@ The Web definitions come from the `dsh-web-app` bundle. Definitions are ordinary
 
 The registry writes no declarations. The `read` Remote renders one declaration’s child list back as entry-list YAML (`!!js` conditions included) so a client can show what a preset composes; nothing accepts YAML back. A new preset or an override of a shipped one is a bundle patch: an `insert` of a `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-preset` row, or a patch keyed by that row’s id, installed into the profile with `plugin_manager`; Creator mode authors such bundles in conversation.
 
+Selection calls the `agent-preset/resolve-selection` waterfall before mounting. Extensions delegate with `next()` and may return a registered derived composition. The registry checks the turn boundary before and after resolution; rejection leaves the current binding and selection log unchanged.
+
+Hidden derived definitions can name a selectable `selectionBase` for mode presentation. `derive()` records and flattens this association when `selectable: false`; registration rejects empty or self-referencing bases and associations on selectable definitions. Reads wait for the Host Loader to settle when the base is absent, because declarations start concurrently, then diagnose missing, hidden, or associated bases and refuse new bindings or selections. Subsequent reads recheck the relation after base removal or replacement; existing revision leases remain retained. The roster exposes the association, while Session selection and logs continue to identify the complete execution composition. Derivation retains the base Loader resolution context and copies plugin rows without parsing display YAML. Do not read diagnostics from inside a Host row's activation: settlement waits for that activation to finish.
+
